@attribute [Route(GlobalValues.Path_Nav_Group_Quirks)]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Page_Title_Nav_Group_Quirks</PageTitle>

<section class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Class @GlobalValues.Info_Box_Coloured_Modifier">
    <h1 class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Nav Group Quirks & Issues</h1>

    <p>
        Below are all the quirks and/or issues that I experienced whilst testing the Nav Group component.
    </p>

</section>

<section class="section-box">
    <h2 id="screen-reader-quirks" class="@GlobalValues.Info_Box_Heading_Class">Screen reader quirks</h2>
    <ul aria-labelledby="screen-reader-quirks">
        <li>
            <b>Narrator</b> more often than not will not announce that the section item has been expanded after activation when
            parried with either Edge or Chrome, but is fine when paired with Firefox.
        </li>
        <li>
            <b>JAWS</b> paired with Firefox will sometimes repeat section names and actions (expanded/collapsed).
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p style="margin-top:1rem;">
        <strong>Note: </strong> The same quirks were also noted in the ARIA Authoring Practices Guide (APG) disclosure examples.
    </p>
</section>


<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Left_Arrow_Modifier" href="@GlobalValues.Path_Nav_Group_Overview">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Main_Nav_Section_Heading_Nav_Group - @GlobalValues.Page_Heading_Nav_Group_Overview</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Right_Arrow_Modifier" href="@GlobalValues.Path_SkipTo_Overview">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Main_Nav_Section_Heading_SkipTo - @GlobalValues.Page_Heading_Skipto_Overview</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
</div>
